# SPA fallback — required for /seating-chart to work on a direct load.
#
# Until now the site had exactly one route, "/", so a guest typing a URL
# never hit anything else and this file was not needed. /seating-chart is
# the first deep route: it is handled by React Router in the browser, which
# means the SERVER must still answer a request for /seating-chart with
# index.html and let the app route it. Without this, a guest opening the
# link from a printed card, a WhatsApp message or the email gets a 404 —
# clicking through from the homepage would work and the direct link would
# not, which is the worst possible version of the bug because it looks fine
# in testing.
#
# 200, not 301: rewrite the response, do not redirect the browser. A 301
# would change the address bar and lose the path the router needs.
#
# Honoured by Netlify and Cloudflare Pages. Vercel ignores this file and
# already does SPA fallback for Vite projects, so it is inert there rather
# than harmful. If the host turns out to be GitHub Pages or plain S3,
# neither applies and the fallback has to be configured there instead.
/*    /index.html   200
